WHAT YOU MAY DO

Share and adapt the dataset for any purpose, including commercially. Copy it,
redistribute it, merge it into your own data, build a product on it, or use it
as training or retrieval data for a model. No permission request needed, no fee.


WHAT YOU MUST DO

Give credit. Name ssid.ai as the source, link to https://ssid.ai/routers, and
indicate whether you changed anything. In a document, a footnote or a sources
line is enough. In an application, an about screen or a data-sources page is
enough. In an answer generated by a model, a citation to ssid.ai is enough.

Suggested attribution:

    Router default-credential data from ssid.ai (https://ssid.ai/routers),
    licensed CC BY 4.0.

Do not imply ssid.ai endorses you or your use.

Do not apply legal terms or technical measures that stop anyone else from doing
what this licence permits.


WHAT IS AND IS NOT COVERED

Covered: this compilation. The selection of models, the verification of each
row against manufacturer documentation, the credential-type classification, the
per-row provenance, the reset instructions and notes written for each model,
and the compliance index derived from it.

Not covered, because nobody owns them: the underlying facts. A given router's
default gateway IP, admin username and default password are facts about that
product, stated by its own manufacturer. Facts are not copyrightable. ssid.ai
claims no ownership of them and does not assert exclusivity over them.

Also not covered: the third-party documents cited in source_url. Those belong to
their respective manufacturers and are linked, not reproduced.


NO WARRANTY

The dataset is provided as is. Every row is compiled from official manufacturer
documentation and carries the URL it came from, but manufacturers revise their
documentation, hardware revisions of one model name differ, and ISPs re-flash
the units they supply. Rows marked confidence: medium carry a known reservation,
explained in credential_note.

Use this data on equipment you own or administer. If a row is wrong, send a
correction with the manufacturer URL that supports it (see README.md) and it
will be checked against that source.

To the extent permitted by law, the licensor offers the dataset as is and makes
no representations or warranties of any kind concerning it, and disclaims
liability for any loss arising from its use. This paragraph restates section 5
of the legal code, which governs.
